cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OptiCore Studio in published work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "OptiCore Studio: optical design and simulation in the browser"
abstract: >-
  A browser-based optical design and simulation environment on an independently
  implemented, test-validated Python engine: sequential lens design, analysis,
  optimisation and tolerancing, thin-film coatings, non-sequential stray light and
  illumination, and wave optics (fibre modes, RCWA, physical-optics propagation,
  FDTD).
authors:
  - family-names: Heiskanen
    given-names: Juuso
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/OnemanHobbystudio/opticore-studio"
url: "https://github.com/OnemanHobbystudio/opticore-studio"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - optics
  - optical design
  - lens design
  - ray tracing
  - thin films
  - physical optics
  - optimisation
